'''Porciúncula''' ({{Literal translation|small piece of land}}, {{Lang-kp|Purikána}}) is the administrative seat of the [[regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Jaguarundi]], within the [[Araucaria|Araucarian]] community of [[Balisca]]. It is located near the [[W:Mouth (river)|mouth]] of the [[Guadazequias|Guadazequias river]], and with a population of 713,288 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]], is the most populous city on Araucaria's West Coast.

